{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"agent_message","text":"I found a stale-carry path in the symlink guards: a declared dependency containing `link/..` is cleaned before the guard examines it, but the OS follows the link before applying `..`. That can make the guard and selection track a different input from the one the check reads. This is established by source tracing and an in-memory probe; I couldn’t create a new Git fixture in the read-only sandbox. I’ll finish the remaining sweep before reporting the findings."}}
