{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat .pose/results/pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks-matrix.md; rg -n 'schema|tool_id|artifact-check|closeout-check|assess-design' .pose/review-bundles/rvb-a9fd7334d3cd90f4.json | head -20; nl -ba .pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md | sed -n '188,199p'; cmp POSE.md pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md; cmp locales/pt-BR/POSE.md pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/locales/pt-BR/POSE.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Strict matrix for pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks, round 11\n\nThe [structured result](delivery-validation.json) is the run after the fixes for findings N27–N29 of review round 10. The engine changed, so `--carry` ran everything. It passed.\n2:  \"schema_version\": 1,\n541:          \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n545:            \"artifact-check\",\n560:          \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n631:          \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n635:            \"closeout-check\",\n773:        \"check\": \"assess-design\",\n3430:        \"kind\": \"schema\",\n3433:        \"reason\": \"canonical bundle and attestation schema identity\"\n   188\t  - N25: an enclosing module was not selected when a nested module changed.\n   189\t  - N26: case folding in ancestor directories of a dependency.\n   190\t  All three are fixed, and the lead extended N25 so the root module encloses every module. Each regression test failed when its fix was mutated out.\n   191\t- 2026-11-23: review round 10 (rrn-29af03286365811e) found N27–N29. N27: the case probe failed open on an unusable first entry. N28: dependencies outside the repository were accepted. N29: the ADR and this summary misdescribed the self-contained fallback. All three are fixed; N27 and N28 have regression tests that failed when their fixes were mutated out.\n   192\t\n   193\t### Results summary\n   194\tAll new and existing tests pass, and the strict matrix is green. In this repository, `pose-mcp` holds 233 of the 236 checks and is high criticality, so carrying saves little here. In an instance with many modules, a change confined to one of them reruns that module, the modules enclosing it and its declared dependents. A changed file that no module owns also reruns every module that is not declared self-contained.\n   195\t\n   196\t### Requirement trace\n   197\t- R1 [satisfied] test:TestCarryRefusesIncompatibleFlags\n   198\t- R2 [satisfied] test:TestCarryFallsBackToAFullRun test:TestCarryRefusesAFilteredBase test:TestCarryRefusesABaseThatValidatedADirtyWorkingCopy test:TestEngineIdentityRefusesModifiedBuilds test:TestCarryRefusesModulesReachedThroughASymlink test:TestValidateHeadMovingDuringTheRunIsNotClean test:TestValidateHeadMovingDuringTheRunBindsNoMaterial test:TestCarryRefusesModulesSharingADirectory test:TestCarryPlansAgainstThePinnedHead test:TestCarryRefusesDependenciesReachedThroughASymlink test:TestCarryRefusesASymlinkInsideAModule test:TestCarryRefusesASymlinkFromAModuleToAnUnownedPath test:TestCarryAllowsSymlinksBetweenUnownedPaths test:TestCarryDetectsACaseInsensitiveFilesystem test:TestCarryRefusesDuplicateCheckIDs test:TestValidateUntrackedMaterialCreatedDuringTheRunIsNotClean test:TestCarryRefusesAnAliasingSymlinkInsideASubmodule test:TestCarryDetectsACaseFoldedDirectory test:TestCarryScansAGitlinkInsideAModule test:TestCarryRelevantDirsIncludeEveryAncestor test:TestCarryCaseProbeSkipsUnusableEntries test:TestCarryRefusesDependenciesOutsideTheRepository\n   199\t- R3 [satisfied] test:TestCarryRunsOnlyTheChangedModule test:TestCarryRecordFileIsNotAChange test:TestCarryIgnoresDerivedAdministrativeRecords test:TestCarrySelectsAModuleWithoutAPriorResult\nPOSE.md pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md differ: char 126198, line 577\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"agent_message","text":"A second gap is established: `material_clean` relies on `git status`, which hides tracked edits marked `assume-unchanged` or `skip-worktree`. The repository’s existing snapshot tests demonstrate that blind spot and pass with the stronger snapshot reader, but validate doesn’t use that reader here. I’ll report this and the symlink-resolution gap as blockers to the unchanged-input guarantee."}}
