{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"diff -u POSE.md pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md | head -35; sed -n '530,560p' .pose/review-bundles/rvb-a9fd7334d3cd90f4.json; sed -n '228,280p' pose-mcp/internal/pose/git_snapshot_integrity.go; rg -n 'Test.*(Canonical|Publish|Writer)' pose-mcp/internal/pose/*test.go | rg 'writer|coordin|publish' | head -12\"","aggregated_output":"--- POSE.md\t2026-11-23 05:43:48.233195388 -0300\n+++ pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist/POSE.md\t2026-11-23 05:43:48.273709502 -0300\n@@ -574,19 +574,6 @@\n - assisted execution via [`pose`](pose) (CLI)\n - progressive maturity with skills in [`.agents/skills/`](.agents/skills/)\n \n-## Open-Source POSE Contributor Mode\n-\n-<!-- pose:contributor-mode -->\n-\n-This repository has enabled POSE Contributor Mode. Executing AI agents collaborate on improving POSE engine stability and developer experience under explicit user adjudication.\n-\n-- **Continuous Opportunity Scouting**: On every issue resolution or task execution, proactively scout for related improvements, edge cases, root-level parity gaps, or complementary corrections across adjacent tools and commands.\n-- **User Consent & Explicit Adjudication**: Staging or submitting contributions upstream is ALWAYS an explicit user decision. Agents must ask the user for confirmation before staging drafts under `.pose/contributions/` or opening GitHub issues.\n-- **Lifecycle & Status Integrity**: Track contribution states (`staged` -> `submitted` / `dismissed`) with `pose contribute list --status <staged|submitted|dismissed|all>`, `pose contribute submit <file>`, `pose contribute mark-submitted <file> [--issue-url <url>]`, or `pose contribute dismiss <file>`.\n-- Check contributor status: `pose contribute status`\n-- Stage a contribution manually: `pose contribute stage --type <bug|enhancement> --title <title>`\n-- Disable contributor mode: `pose contribute disable`\n-- Privacy guarantee: staged reports strictly isolate POSE engine mechanics and never leak proprietary code.\n ## Opt-in progressive review profiles (ABM)\n \n Add `engineering-judgment@1` and/or `high-criticality-review@1` explicitly to\n          \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n          \"description\": \"Compare the solution with the smallest sufficient alternative, including negative space, speculative extensibility and the condition that would invalidate the choice.\",\n          \"required\": true,\n          \"kind\": \"judgment\",\n          \"profiles\": [\n            \"structural-materiality@1\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"tools\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n          \"requiredness\": \"required\",\n          \"args\": [\n            \"pose\",\n            \"artifact-check\",\n            \"--spec\",\n            \"pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks\",\n            \"--strict\"\n          ],\n          \"rationale\": \"reconcile declared artifacts with Git-observed provenance\",\n          \"criteria\": [\n            \"requirements\",\n            \"scope\"\n          ],\n          \"preconditions\": [\n            \"artifacts-attributed\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n// of index flags. No refresh/update-index mutation is needed to see hidden edits.\nfunc gitMaterializedChanges(root, commit string) ([]string, error) {\n\treturn gitMaterializedChangesFor(root, commit, nil)\n}\nfunc gitMaterializedChangesFor(root, commit string, matters func(string) bool) ([]string, error) {\n\treturn gitMaterializedChangesForIn(NativeFiles(), root, commit, matters, \"\")\n}\n\nfunc gitMaterializedChangesForIn(files Files, root, commit string, matters func(string) bool, producer string) ([]string, error) {\n\tfiles = FilesOrNative(files)\n\tif producer != \"\" {\n\t\tproducer = governanceProducerFromFiles(files, producer)\n\t}\n\trunGit := func(root string, args ...string) ([]byte, error) {\n\t\tif len(args) == 5 && args[0] == \"ls-tree\" {\n\t\t\treturn listCommittedTree(root, args[4])\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn snapshotGit(root, args...)\n\t}\n\tworktreeIdentity := dispatchWorktreeIdentity\n\tif producer != \"\" {\n\t\trunGit = func(root string, args ...string) ([]byte, error) {\n\t\t\tif len(args) == 5 && args[0] == \"ls-tree\" {\n\t\t\t\t// The governed listing keeps its read-view provenance under the\n\t\t\t\t// listing's own bound and deadline (review N4).\n\t\t\t\tctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), gitTreeListingTimeout)\n\t\t\t\tdefer cancel()\n\t\t\t\treturn CaptureGovernanceGitContextIn(files, ctx, root, producer, gitTreeListingMaxBytes, args...)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\treturn captureGovernanceGit(files, root, producer, args...)\n\t\t}\n\t\tworktreeIdentity = func(root string) (string, error) {\n\t\t\treturn dispatchWorktreeIdentityGoverned(files, root, producer)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tvar err error\n\troot, err = filepath.Abs(root)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil, &GitSnapshotError{\"root\", err}\n\t}\n\tif _, err := worktreeIdentity(root); err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil, err\n\t}\n\tout, err := runGit(root, \"ls-tree\", \"-r\", \"-l\", \"-z\", commit)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn nil, err\n\t}\n\tbudget := gitSnapshotBudget(gitCommittedTreeBytes(out))\n\tvar changed []string\n\tvar total int64\n\tcount := 0\n\tfor _, record := range bytes.Split(out, []byte{0}) {\n\t\tif len(record) == 0 {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/writer_publication_test.go:31:func TestConcurrentPublishersNeverShareStaging(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/writer_publication_test.go:145:func TestATransferWaitsForNoLifecycleWriterOfItsSpecs(t *testing.T) {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/writer_publication_test.go:171:func TestStartRefusesWhileAnotherLifecycleWriterHoldsItsSpec(t *testing.T) {\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
