{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"web_search","id":"exec-102568c8-badc-4f53-b638-a6fb5a8d7258","query":"site.developer.apple.com APFS normalization insensitive case sensitive Unicode filenames","action":{"type":"search","query":"site.developer.apple.com APFS normalization insensitive case sensitive Unicode filenames"},"results":[{"type":"text_result","domain":"developer.apple.com","ref_id":"turn0search0","snippet":"Most disks attached to Apple devices use Apple File System (APFS) for the underlying disk format. ... APFS is case insensitive by default, but people","title":"Files and directories | Apple Developer Documentation","url":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/technologyoverviews/files-and-directories"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"developer.apple.com","ref_id":"turn0search1","snippet":"How does Apple File System handle filenames? ... Being normalization-insensitive ensures that normalization variants of a filename cannot be created in the same directory, and","title":"Frequently Asked Questions","url":"https://developer.apple.com/library/archive/documentation/FileManagement/Conceptual/APFS_Guide/FAQ/FAQ.html"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"usermanual.wiki","ref_id":"turn0search12","snippet":"(APFS_INCOMPAT_CASE_INSENSITIVE \\ ... | APFS_INCOMPAT_NORMALIZATION_INSENSITIVE \\ ... 2020-06-22 | Copyright © 2020 Apple Inc.","title":"Apple File System Reference","url":"https://usermanual.wiki/m/c99e56fa3180a03a5e2543af4ab9965150b60554f67b790515fabcffb409e203.pdf"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.rfc-editor.org","ref_id":"turn0search13","snippet":"Filename Normalization ... - New Technology File System (NTFS) and Apple’s Hierarchical File System (HFS) Plus usually preserve case when storing files but are case","title":"RFC 8493  BagIt  October 2018","url":"https://www.rfc-editor.org/pdfrfc/rfc8493.txt.pdf"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"developer.apple.com","ref_id":"turn0search2","snippet":"Bundle objects always consider case when searching for resource files, even on file systems that support case-insensitive filenames. ... When locating resource files, the bundle","title":"Bundle | Apple Developer Documentation","url":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/Foundation/Bundle?changes=_10"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"developer.apple.com","ref_id":"turn0search3","snippet":"NSFileProviderActions.h states: \"Collision checks should be case insensitive even if the filesystem or file provider might allow two coexisting filenames differing only by their case.\"","title":"File Provider: case-insensitive co… | Apple Developer Forums","url":"https://developer.apple.com/forums/thread/822980"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"github.com","ref_id":"turn0search4","snippet":"case-sensitive APFS volumes. ... \\item[\\texttt{APFS} (case-insensitive).] ... \\texttt{normalization\\_insensitive = false}. ... and Unicode case-fold applied before normalisation on ... wrong lookup-by","title":"apfs-fastindex/docs/manual/chapters/09-names.tex at main · NicoNekoru/apfs-fastindex · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/NicoNekoru/apfs-fastindex/blob/main/docs/manual/chapters/09-names.tex"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"developer.apple.com","ref_id":"turn0search5","snippet":"Bundle objects always consider case when searching for resource files, even on file systems that support case-insensitive filenames. ... When locating resource files, the bundle","title":"NSBundle | Apple Developer Documentation","url":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/foundation/bundle?changes=l_3&language=objc"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"developer.apple.com","ref_id":"turn0search6","snippet":"However, the rules for path equivalence are file-system–specific and have additional considerations like case insensitivity, Unicode normalization, and symbolic links.","title":"FilePath | Apple Developer Documentation","url":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/System/FilePath"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"developer-rno.apple.com","ref_id":"turn0search7","snippet":"When searching or comparing filenames, always assume that the underlying file system is case sensitive. macOS supports many file systems that use case to differentiate","title":"Accessing Files and Directories","url":"https://developer-rno.apple.com/library/archive/documentation/FileManagement/Conceptual/FileSystemProgrammingGuide/AccessingFilesandDirectories/AccessingFilesandDirectories.html"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"developer.apple.com","ref_id":"turn0search8","snippet":"A Boolean value that indicates whether the volume format treats upper and lower case characters in file and directory names as different. ... A Boolean","title":"volumeSupportsCaseSensitiveNames | Apple Developer Documentation","url":"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/foundation/urlresourcevalues/volumesupportscasesensitivenames"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"docs.remotestore.dev","ref_id":"turn0search9","snippet":"* APFS (FAQ): \"APFS accepts only valid UTF-8 encoded filenames for creation, and preserves both case and normalization of the filename on disk in all","title":"What each backend's authority allows in a path or key - remote-store","url":"https://docs.remotestore.dev/latest/explanation/design/research/research-backend-path-authorities/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"manuals.plus","ref_id":"turn0search14","snippet":"#define APFS_SUPPORTED_INCOMPAT_MASK (APFS_INCOMPAT_CASE_INSENSITIVE \\ ... | APFS_INCOMPAT_NORMALIZATION_INSENSITIVE \\ ... 2020-06-22 | Copyright © 2020 Apple Inc.","title":"Apple File System Reference","url":"https://manuals.plus/m/c99e56fa3180a03a5e2543af4ab9965150b60554f67b790515fabcffb409e203.pdf"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"apple-docs.everest.mt","ref_id":"turn0search10","snippet":"You can represent this as the Unicode hex f1 character. ... So in order to rectify this, we're introducing two new normalization schemes for Apple","title":"WWDC2017 Session 715 — Apple Developer Docs","url":"https://apple-docs.everest.mt/docs/wwdc/wwdc2017-715"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"developer.apple.com","ref_id":"turn0search11","snippet":"Providing a filename extension for your application’s data files makes it easier for end users to exchange your data files with users on other platforms.","title":"File System Guidelines","url":"https://developer.apple.com/library/archive/documentation/MacOSX/Conceptual/BPFileSystem/Articles/FileSystemGuidelines.html"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"devstreaming-cdn.apple.com","ref_id":"turn0search15","snippet":"Unicode and APFS ... Three large dashed rounded-square boxes on a black background illustrate Unicode filename forms.","title":"715_WhatsNewinAppleFileSystem_02_D.key","url":"https://devstreaming-cdn.apple.com/videos/wwdc/2017/715gk347h3udl/715/715_whats_new_in_apple_file_system.pdf?dl=1"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"ftp.funet.fi","ref_id":"turn0search16","snippet":"Filename Normalization ... - New Technology File System (NTFS) and Apple’s Hierarchical File System (HFS) Plus usually preserve case when storing files but are case","title":"RFC 8493 — BagIt — October 2018","url":"https://ftp.funet.fi/pub/standards/RFC/rfc8493.txt.pdf"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"en.wikipedia.org","ref_id":"turn0search17","snippet":"In filesystems in Unix-like systems, filenames are usually case-sensitive (there can be separate readme.txt and Readme.txt files in the same directory). MacOS is somewhat unusual","title":"Case sensitivity","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Case_sensitivity"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"en.wikipedia.org","ref_id":"turn0search18","snippet":"Developer | Apple Inc. ... Among these limitations, it does not perform Unicode normalization while HFS+ does, leading to problems with languages other than English.","title":"Apple File System","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple_File_System"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"en.wikipedia.org","ref_id":"turn0search19","snippet":"This means two separate files might be created with the same text filename and a different byte implementation of the filename, such as L\"\\x00C0.txt\" (UTF-16,","title":"Filename","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Filename"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"de.wikipedia.org","ref_id":"turn0search20","snippet":"Die von macOS verwendeten Dateisysteme HFS+ und APFS (ab macOS High Sierra) werden standardmäßig case-insensitive verwendet, können aber umgeschaltet werden. ... * xahlee.org: On Unix","title":"Case sensitivity","url":"https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Case_sensitivity"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"de.wikipedia.org","ref_id":"turn0search21","snippet":"Die meisten aktuellen Dateisysteme sind jedoch in jedem Fall case-preserving, das heißt, sie halten den Dateinamen in der bei der Erstellung oder Umbenennung benutzten Schreibweise","title":"Dateiname","url":"https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dateiname"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"en.wikipedia.org","ref_id":"turn0search22","snippet":"Most of the file systems in macOS, current versions of Microsoft Windows, and all versions of Amiga OS are case-preserving and case-insensitive. ... Most of","title":"Case preservation","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Case_preservation"}]}}
