{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_65","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\nThe four prior findings are fixed for their reported cases. Three high-severity blockers remain:\n\n- **R10-N30 — Symlink traversal is cleaned before inspection**, at [validate_carry.go:313](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-695147164/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:313). With `unowned/link -> ../other/deep`, a declared dependency `unowned/link/../input` resolves physically to `other/input`. The guards and selection instead use `unowned/input`. A change to `other/input` can therefore leave a self-contained consumer carrying a stale pass. Reject ambiguous traversal or establish physical path identity before cleaning. Established by source tracing, an in-memory selection probe, and a read-only OS path-resolution probe; no new Git fixture was created.\n- **R10-N31 — `material_clean` trusts status-hidden edits**, at [validate.go:1435](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-695147164/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1435). Both cleanliness helpers rely on `git status`, which hides edits marked `assume-unchanged` or `skip-worktree`. A baseline can pass over a hidden uncommitted fix, record `material_clean: true`, then supply a stale carried pass after the committed failing content is restored. The existing snapshot regressions demonstrate this status blind spot and passed. Use content-based comparison with the recorded commit.\n- **R10-N32 — Unicode filename aliases evade the case guards**, at [validate_carry.go:496](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-695147164/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go:496). On case-sensitive APFS, `shared/café.txt` and its decomposed spelling resolve to the same file. A consumer declaring one spelling can miss a change reported under the other. Case swapping does not detect this. Apple documents normalization insensitivity for case-sensitive APFS. This finding is based on source analysis and documented platform behavior, not an APFS fixture run. [Apple APFS FAQ](https://developer.apple.com/library/archive/documentation/FileManagement/Conceptual/APFS_Guide/FAQ/FAQ.html)\n\nBoth strict validation invocations, the artifact check, and focused source tests passed. These results do not cover the three sequences above. The installed `pose` runner predates the patch; the focused Go tests compiled the reviewed source directly. Assessments were skipped because the read-only filesystem prevented creating a scratch copy. The checkout remains unchanged; no attestation was recorded.\n\nRules applied: the review workflow, backend Go, security, documentation style, and delivery-evidence rules. Reviewed bundle: `rvb-2fe1866df7ce04ff`, digest `sha256:2fe1866df7ce04ff45796cb0702e0fca60dd5d64fe4ef05e302ee3bc8f8f34af`.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R8-N26\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate_carry.go:444-470 now enumerates every existing ancestor through the repository root. TestCarryRelevantDirsIncludeEveryAncestor passed in the focused carry test run. Unicode normalization aliases are a separate remaining issue, R10-N32.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R9-N27\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate_carry.go:480-497 treats ReadDir failure conservatively and continues past unusable original entries. TestCarryCaseProbeSkipsUnusableEntries passed in the focused carry test run.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R9-N28\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate_carry.go:141-148 refuses absolute and lexically root-escaping dependencies. TestCarryRefusesDependenciesOutsideTheRepository passed for the quoted ../shared/input and absolute-path cases. Compound symlink traversal is reported separately as R10-N30.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R9-N29\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \".pose/adr/2026-11-22-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:25 and .pose/specs/2026-11-22-pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks.md:194 now distinguish module-local selection from the unowned-file fallback.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R10-N30\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go\",\n      \"line\": 313,\n      \"summary\": \"Cleaning dependencies before inspecting symlink traversal loses physical input identity. For modules a and b, declare b selfContained with dependsOn=[\\\"unowned/link/../input\\\"], track unowned/link -> ../other/deep, and keep other/deep and other/input outside discovered modules. The OS reads other/input, but aliasingSymlinkIn, carryRelevantDirs and declaredDependencyHits use unowned/input. Neither the link nor its lexical target intersects that cleaned dependency, so eligibility succeeds. Changing other/input can carry b's stale pass. Resolve and confine traversal before cleaning, or conservatively refuse ambiguous paths; also examine the analogous target cleaning at line 347. Established by source tracing, an in-memory predicate probe, and read-only verification that /bin/../local resolves differently from its lexical cleaning on this host. A new Git fixture could not be created in the read-only sandbox.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R10-N31\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\",\n      \"line\": 1435,\n      \"summary\": \"material_clean can certify content that differs from the recorded commit. materialWorktreeClean at line 1699 and materialTrackedUnchanged at line 1732 only inspect Git status, which hides tracked edits marked assume-unchanged or skip-worktree. Mark b's failing input with either flag, apply an uncommitted passing fix, run a full baseline, restore the failing committed content, clear the flag and commit only the canonical record. The baseline records material_clean=true, and --carry sees only an excluded record change and can reuse the false pass. TestGitSnapshotHiddenEditsAndTypes passed and explicitly demonstrates status returning no changes for both flags while the content reader detects divergence; TestGitSnapshotSubmoduleHiddenEditIsNotClean also passed. Use content-based comparison against the pinned commit for base certification and current eligibility, retaining conservative administrative exclusions.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R10-N32\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_carry.go\",\n      \"line\": 496,\n      \"summary\": \"Case probes do not establish that lexical filename comparison is sound on normalization-insensitive filesystems. Case-sensitive APFS resolves NFC shared/café.txt and NFD shared/cafe\\\\u0301.txt to the same file, while declaredDependencyHits compares those strings byte-for-byte. A self-contained b declaring the NFD dependency can pass a baseline, then retain that pass after the NFC Git path changes. The case probes and module-directory alias check need not refuse this repository. Detect normalization aliases or compare dependency identity consistently before allowing carry. Apple documents normalization insensitivity in both APFS case variants at https://developer.apple.com/library/archive/documentation/FileManagement/Conceptual/APFS_Guide/FAQ/FAQ.html . Established by source review, the documented platform contract and an in-memory normalization/selection probe; not exercised on APFS hardware.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Swept the complete implementation subject against R1-R10 and D1-D3: argument compatibility; base schema, mode, engine and ancestry checks; cancellation and failure preservation; pinned-head and working-copy certification; administrative exclusions; rename and unusual-name handling; gitlinks, submodules and their symlinks; symlink traversal; case and Unicode path aliases; declared dependency confinement and transitive widening; root and nested ownership; manifest-free moduleOverrides; stack/check identity changes; criticality widening; chained carry origins; delivery parsing; concurrent dispatch and atomic canonical publication; help, English and pt-BR manuals and scaffold copies. All four listed prior findings were accounted for before reporting new findings. Focused carry/scope, delivery-parser, concurrency/cancellation, publication and hidden-edit tests passed. Both strict matrix invocations completed successfully. The installed pose runner is revision 40019024deed61f74466cf49d64b2994b4b4f7c5; reviewed source is 392d81f70007476e8eb264ae86f954a7e6f879f8. Focused Go tests compile the reviewed source. Assessment scratch creation failed with a read-only-filesystem error, so no assessments were run on the sealed checkout. Recurrence check reported zero flagged keys. No repository changes or attestation were made. The cheapest false satisfaction of the new evidence gate remains certifying status-clean as material-clean, demonstrated by R10-N31; the existing adversarial corpus does not cover this carry sequence.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R10-N31\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Verified the explicit selfContained risk and D1 premise. Git-status cleanliness does not prove commit-equivalent content. APFS behavior is documented but was not exercised locally.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/validate-concurrent-steps-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected silent carried-entry dispatch, cancellation, loaded-base immutability and guarded atomic publication. Focused concurrency, cancellation and publication tests passed, including TestConcurrentPublishersNeverShareStaging.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The new result fields are additive. Delivery parsing preserves legacy behavior and reads carried head/time when present; TestDeliveryValidationRunReadsTheCarriedHead passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R10-N30\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ambiguous dependency traversal is accepted instead of producing the conservative full-run fallback.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R10-N31\",\n      \"rationale\": \"A false material-clean certificate can propagate stale carried outcomes into canonical delivery evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected carry.used/reason, base and selected-module context, per-check origin/time, counts and fallback output. These expose carry decisions without adding inherited environment values to results.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined CLI refusals and additive schema-1 fields. Old records retain their reading behavior and cannot become carry bases without the required new fields; no MCP transport contract was changed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R10-N31\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Passing existing tests does not establish unchanged inputs in the hidden-edit sequence. R10-N30 and R10-N32 establish additional stale-carry paths.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R10-N30\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reusing changed-scope selection addresses repeated full validation, but D1 requires physical input equivalence. Lexical cleaning and case-only probes leave that premise unproved.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-253b523c\",\n          \"basis\": \"D1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The added ADR records the decision to preserve historical per-check origins while binding the aggregate run at HEAD, conditional on selection proving that carried inputs are unchanged.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined help, English and pt-BR manuals, scaffold changes, ADR consequences and the corrected spec summary. They describe the intended contract and current selection rules; the remaining eligibility defects are reported separately.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Examined invalid flag combinations, canonical-path refusals, missing or incompatible bases and explain output. Detected eligibility failures provide actionable reasons and widen to execution.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R10-N31\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R2's commit-equivalent material condition and D1 are not established. R10-N30 and R10-N32 also break R2/R3's unchanged-input guarantee.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-9198072c5206e634\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared the spec artifacts and decisions with the implementation range. Changes remain within validation planning, result representation, delivery reading, regression coverage and the corresponding governance/docs.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"R10-N30\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The evidence authority boundary depends on safe input attribution. Lexical dependency inspection does not establish physical confinement or identity; R10-N31 also permits false certification of the recorded material.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-9198072c5206e634\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared reuse of existing module selection and whole-matrix/engine identity with per-check input manifests and manual record merging. The selected granularity avoids a new arbitrary-input declaration system and preserves existing outcomes. Its suitability depends on conservative refusal wherever path identity cannot be established; broader reuse would require reconsidering that choice.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks --strict --json\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completed with no error/critical findings. The JSON contained 985 repository-wide orphan warnings. The filtered command completed with exit 0.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Read the spec, ADR and sealed design evidence directly. A scratch copy could not be created on the read-only filesystem; assessment commands were not run on the sealed checkout.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Scratch creation failed with a read-only-filesystem error. Did not run a persisting assessment against the sealed checkout.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Attempted to prepare a scratch copy for assessment execution, but mktemp was denied. Reviewed the file consumer and used the sealed integration evidence and focused parser test.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Scratch creation was denied, so the assessment was not executed. No assessment output was written to the sealed checkout.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion tool requires the review conclusion to be recorded first. This independent review was explicitly prohibited from recording an attestation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion tool requires the review conclusion to be recorded first. POSE must record and verify the returned draft.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Resolved backend-go with security and documentation-style rules; read and applied those rules and the delivery-evidence rule.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran pose validate --strict successfully: 236 steps passed and Result: SUCCESS. The installed runner predates the patch; its matrix launches current repository test commands. The cited reference is the bundle's sealed canonical result.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Ran pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp successfully with exit 0. Also ran focused Go tests against the reviewed source for carry/scope, engine identity, delivery parsing, concurrency/cancellation, canonical publication and hidden Git edits. The cited reference is the bundle's sealed canonical result.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
